* lsk489.lib - Linear Systems LSK489, dual monolithic N-channel JFET.
* VENDOR MODEL, TRANSCRIBED BY HAND FROM A VENDOR PDF (ADR-013).
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/jfet/lsk489.lib
*   J1 drain gate source LSK489A
*
* The LSK489 is a DUAL: one package holds two matched devices on the
* same die. This file provides the model for ONE device - instantiate it
* twice for a pair. There is no KiCad symbol for the dual yet (L10).
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. The full story is in
* models/jfet/lsk489.provenance.json and in
* docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-09-L6-trascrizione-lsk489.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Linear Systems publishes this model as a PDF containing the .MODEL
* text, not as a .lib. ADR-013 accepted that transcription burden
* knowingly and made the method binding: TWO INDEPENDENT READINGS THAT
* MUST AGREE. Both were done on the frozen copy at
* vendor/jfet/linear_systems/LSK489/Copy_LSK489A_NJF.pdf and came out
* byte-identical (a third, pdftotext, agreed too).
*
* The vendor line, VERBATIM, is:
*
*   .model LSK489A NJF(Beta=2.2m Betatce=-.5 Rd=11 Rs=30 Lambda=4.3m Vto=-1.13
*   Vtotc=-2.5m Is=3f Isr=0 N=1 Xti=0 Alpha=30u VK=120 Cgd=3.19p Mj=0.32 Pb=0.8 Fc=0.5
*   Cgs=2.92p Kf=0.0009f Af=1 Gdsnoi=2.15 Nlev=3 Mfg=Linear_Systems)
*
* ONE thing was removed, and only one: Mfg=Linear_Systems. ngspice does
* not know that parameter, evaluates the value as an expression, and
* dies - "Undefined parameter [linear_systems]", "ERROR: fatal error in
* ngspice". That failure is LOUD, not silent. Nothing else was changed:
* no value was rounded, reordered or "corrected".
*
* FOUR parameters below are accepted by ngspice and then IGNORED, with a
* warning on every run: isr, alpha, vk, mj. They are PSpice/LTspice
* refinements of the gate junction and the saturation current. They are
* kept deliberately - the diff from the vendor text stays minimal, and a
* simulator that does support them gets the vendor's own values. The
* warnings are expected output, not a defect to chase.
*
* The parameters that matter for NC-004 - Kf, Af, Nlev, Gdsnoi - ARE
* accepted. That is the whole point of this file: the placeholder models
* in spice/preamp/placeholder_devices.lib have KF = 0, so they have no
* 1/f noise at all and every noise figure taken from them is a floor,
* not a prediction.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* SUFFIXES: docs/limitations.md #13 does NOT bite here - checked
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* #13 is that "1M" means 1 megohm in KiCad and 1 milliohm in SPICE, six
* orders of magnitude with no error from either tool. Every suffix in
* this model was checked against it and every one is unambiguous:
*
*   2.2m  4.3m  -2.5m   -> milli in both conventions
*   3f    0.0009f       -> femto
*   3.19p 2.92p         -> pico
*   30u                 -> micro
*
* This is written down precisely BECAUSE the values are right: this is
* the spot where a later reader, remembering #13, would "fix" a correct
* number. Do not. The transcription is verified against the vendor PDF.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET IN L7 - THE VERDICT IS MIXED
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Step 4 of ADR-013 was done on 2026-09-09. Full record, with every
* deck and all three independent legs, in
* docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-09-L7-controllo-incrociato-lsk489.md.
*
* Measured AT THE DATASHEET'S OWN TEST CONDITIONS - which is half the
* check, and the half L6 had explicitly left open - against LSK489A
* window, datasheet RevA40 page 2, all at 25 C:
*
*   I_DSS      2.59283 mA  (VDG = 15 V, VGS = 0)
*              window 2.5 / 5.5 / 8.5 mA
*              -> INSIDE, but 3.7% above the minimum and 52.9% below
*                 typical.
*
*   V_GS(off)  -1.124355 V (VDS = 15 V, I_D = 1 nA)
*              window -1.5 V min, -3.5 V max
*              -> OUTSIDE. 0.376 V short of the minimum magnitude, 25%.
*
*   V_GS       -0.650211 V (VDS = 15 V, I_D = 500 uA)
*              window -0.5 / -3.5 V
*              -> INSIDE.
*
* THIS IS NOT A TRANSCRIPTION ERROR, and that was measured rather than
* argued. Inside the model I_DSS and V_P are not independent - Beta ties
* them together. Holding the transcribed Beta = 2.2m and moving only
* Vto: -1.13 V gives 2.593 mA, -1.50 V (the datasheet's own V_GS(off)
* minimum) gives 4.392 mA, comfortably inside the A window. So the two
* datasheet windows are mutually consistent and this model sits below
* BOTH, coherently: ONE corner offset, not two independent errors. A
* mis-transcribed Vto would have moved I_DSS and V_P in uncorrelated
* directions. The discrepancy is between the vendor's SPICE model and
* the vendor's own datasheet - not between the PDF and this file.
*
* WHAT IT MEANS: this model describes a LOW-I_DSS CORNER part, not a
* typical one. Bias points computed with it in Fase 4 are a corner case;
* real parts will show higher transconductance. Recorded as NC-013 in
* docs/preamp/NONCOMPLIANCE.md (major, not blocking), closed by L20.
* ADR-013 was NOT reopened: its "reopen if the cross-check does not
* return" clause is about a wrong part or a wrong transcription, and
* neither is the case here.
*
* THE DATASHEET REVISION QUESTION IS CLOSED, by dissolution: there is
* only one revision and it is RevA40. The frozen PDF is NAMED
* LSK489DSRevA38.pdf because that is the filename the manufacturer's
* server sends, but its own footer says "Rev# A40, 04/12/2022" on all 7
* pages. See vendor/jfet/linear_systems/LSK489/PROVENANCE-L7-addendum.json.
*
* The recipe in scripts/validate_models.py is no longer a smoke test: it
* now measures all three at the datasheet's conditions and LOCKS them to
* the values above. It does not claim datasheet conformance, because for
* V_GS(off) there is none.

.model LSK489A NJF(Beta=2.2m Betatce=-.5 Rd=11 Rs=30 Lambda=4.3m Vto=-1.13
+ Vtotc=-2.5m Is=3f Isr=0 N=1 Xti=0 Alpha=30u VK=120 Cgd=3.19p Mj=0.32 Pb=0.8 Fc=0.5
+ Cgs=2.92p Kf=0.0009f Af=1 Gdsnoi=2.15 Nlev=3)
